WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.640
Well we'd love to see as many&nbsp;
people as possible here at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.800
old Bluff Cemetery in Lagan Street&nbsp;
on the 8th of November. The Cemetery was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.080
brought into being on December of 1860, with&nbsp;
the first internment of a two-year-old child&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:26.320
Here we have the final resting place of&nbsp;
a ship's carpenter that was lost in the Bluff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:33.200
harbour by drowning from the Timaru. Very&nbsp;
fitting that it is the only one in the cemetery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:40.000
with a timber fence around it and a timber&nbsp;
cross and it is of a scotsman William Moyer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:49.040
who died in December just right on Christmas in&nbsp;
1898. He left behind his parents back in Scotland.

